In Ubuntu, the package manager is called APT.
- Package = software or application.
- Repository = a trusted software collection.
- APT = the tool that installs and manages packages.
For example, instead of downloading Nginx manually, you can install it with one command.

sudo apt update	        Refreshes the package list
sudo apt upgrade	Upgrades installed software
sudo apt install nginx	Installs Nginx
sudo apt remove nginx	Removes Nginx
sudo apt purge nginx	Removes Nginx and its system configuration files
sudo apt autoremove	Removes unused dependencies
apt search nginx	Searches for packages
apt show nginx	        Shows package details
nginx -v                verify the version
curl http://localhost   Test you web server
